Woodpecker is a CI/CD engine: pipelines are YAML files in the repository,
run on every push, pull request, tag or schedule from a Git forge
(Forgejo, Gitea, GitHub, GitLab or Bitbucket).

This package is the agent, which takes pipelines from a Woodpecker
server (devel/woodpecker) and runs them. On FreeBSD it uses the local
backend: steps run directly on the host, with the tools installed there.
